        "date": "August 14, 2026",
        "title": "How to make packaging look less meh",
        "subtitle": "Your packaging has one job before anything else: make people want to look twice. It does not need to be loud, expensive, or covered in glitter. It just to feel elevated. Here is how to get there without regretting your bill.",
        "featured_image": "shopify://shop_images/blogFeature.webp",
        "toc_title": "In this post",
        "intro_content": "<p>Most packaging is not ugly. It is undecided. Someone pressed a box because it fit, picked tape because it was in the cupboard, and put a sticker on because they were stickers floating around. Nothing in it is wrong, exactly. It just does not read as thought-out.</p><p>That is the actual gap between packaging that looks cheap and packaging that looks considered... not budget, decidedness. The good news is that decidedness is far cheaper than it looks, and you can usually buy it with one component rather than all of them.</p>",
